n=19: H(rotational)=1184212824763  H(Paley)=1172695746915  -> rotational wins: True
CROSSOVER: Paley's pseudorandomness wins for SHORT cycles / small n; the half-turn's
clustered long-range structure wins for LONG cycles / large n. Paley maximal only n<=11.

HALF-TURN: rotational R_n (i beats next (n-1)/2) = THM-374 half-turn circular tournament
= the LRC half-turn comparator. So the H-maximizer (n>=13) IS the LRC geometry.
